JED has a good EDT emulation.  I have been told that of the freely available
editors, JED's EDT emulation is the best.  Please note that JED does not
emulate the command line mode of EDT nor does it understand EDTINI.EDT
files.  However, it is programmable in a C-like language.  In fact, the
entire EDT emulation is written in the editor extension language.

JED runs on MSDOS, VMS, Unix, and OS/2.  It also runs on DEC ALPHA systems.
The latest version is 0.97-5b from amy.tch.harvard.edu in pub/jed.  I have
also been informed that a newsgroup (alt.lang.s-lang) devoted to JED and its
extension language has been created in Europe and has been sited in Canada.
