Have you tried xvgr (also known as ACE/gr or xmgr)?  Xvgr is a PD program
by Paul J Turner.  It provides a LOT of functionality, with a fairly simple
to use graphical interface (as well as a command line interface).  As far
as I am aware, the only limitation to the size of a single data set is the
amount of memory available for it to use.  (I have done 100,000 point plots
without any problems :-)
I prefer it to gnuplot primarily because it is (for me) much easier to use
--- I can get what I want quickly and easily.  I find the output quite
"pretty", but you will need to see, and experiment for yourself.
Xvgr provides output in PostScript, HPGL, and FrameMaker .mif formats (but
I have only used the PS output, and I have had no problems with including
the graphs into my LaTeX documents.
The version I use is version 2.09 (coincidence?) and runs on a Sun machine.
Unfortunately, I have no idea where it came from (SysOp can't remember), so
I would suggest that you try Archie if you are interested.
Perhaps some other people might know a bit more about it?


