Oh, I forgot to mention that /etc/securettys controls which terminals
are considered secure for root login.  This replaces the ability to
declare the security of terminals in /etc/ttys in Ultrix.  Our
securettys file has:

/dev/console
local:0
:0

I'm assuming that the :0 entry allows login through xdm.  



