I have a DEC 2100/A500MP running OSF/1 3.0 with Enhanced Security
enabled.  We generate from 5 to 600 accounts a day on the system.  Therefore,
the GUI XIsso and XSysAdmin tools must be replaced with an automated
Account Management System.  We did the same thing on our ULTRIX box.  My
problem is the encrypted pw, generated via crypt(), for the protected password
database appears to fail for passwords that are over 8 characters.  The
limited documentation in the man pages and /usr/include/*.h files
indicate the encrypted password is generated in segments.  WHAT IS THE
ACTUAL SCHEME DEC USES?

ps.  XIsso and XSysAdmin are slow.  I have not determined if it is a problem
with the clients and/or server.

ps2.  It sure would be nice if the hashed index /etc/passwd file could 
have entries added without being totally rebuilt.  For a small user base,
rebuilding the passwd database presents only a small problem.  However,
a database with 14,000 users takes a minute or so to rebuild.  This causes
problems with email and other normal system functions.  1) The getpw* routines
should be enhanced to suspend requests if the database is being modified.
2) permit updates to the database without having to totally rebuild.
Unfortunately, I am forced to disable login and sendmail while rebuilding 
the passwd database via mkpasswd.

