Just to clarify (hopefully): I had no luck with my old V1.3 binary of
syd.  However, the "syd" pointer in:

	http://www.dec.com/info/misc/pub-domain-osf1.txt.html

will lead to source that does compile and work under V3.0.

In the case you still want a working top, a patch is now available
via anonymous ftp from:

	ftp://cage.cs.arizona.edu/pub/davidm/top-beta3.3+alpha.patch-v3.0

The patch is relative to top-beta3.3+alpha.tar.Z (also available via
the pub-domain-osf1.txt.html page).  It fixes the lastpid problem that
Burkhard mentioned (although in a slighty different manner: lastpid is
now simply the highest pid that top finds will preparing the display).
It also fixes a bug in computing process states and in computing
whether a process is swapped out.  The original version used an
uninitialized variable to determine whether a process is swapped out.
The patch fixes this to use RSS==0 instead (this isn't the proper
algorithm either, but I didn't find a way to access a process's INCORE
flag via table() in the little time I was willing to spend on top).

In summary, I think it's better to use syd for now, as it provides
more information and is probably less buggy than the patched beta
version of top.

	--david
