It's even more simple than that!  All programs read articles via the
same call in the INN source.  Modify that one routine to check for a
.gz file if the article isn't found.  Then, to do the compression just
do this every 6 hours:

	cd /var/spool/news
	gfind . -regex '.*/[0-9][0-9]*$' -mtime +1 -print | xargs gzip -9

This way you get (1) minimal code changes, (2) fast access to
recent news.

This is another opportunity for someone to become famous by writing
a minimal amount of code.

