>Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec
>From: mccarthyd@csvax.cosc.brocku.ca (David McCarthy)
>Subject: Console port access
>
>I have an alpha 3000 Model 300L and would like to hookup an APC SmartUPS
>to the console port. The 300L manual says the port is fixed at 9600 baud.
>The APC people tell me that their port on the UPS goes at 2400 baud. As
>you can guess there is no communication going on between the APC daemon
>and the UPS. Does anyone have a workaround?
>Dave McCarthy


	That information, from page 6-4 of the DEC 3000 Model 300/300L AXP
Harware Reference Guide, applies only to the port when used as an alternate
console while the system is operating in "console" mode.

	Once an operating system, OpenVMS or OSF/1, is booted the port is 
under the control of the OS and can be set to any of the normal bit rates.
