Thanks to those who replied with helpful suggestions. The problem seemed to
be that you can't just run a program from an init script by re-directing
all its output channels and backgrounding it with &. The program itself
needs to explicitly give up its controlling terminal (setsid()). While I
was doing this I also made it fork itself and use syslog rather than 
fprintf(stderr,...). The program, and I, are now much happier :-)

Andrew

