>danpop@cernapo.cern.ch (Dan Pop) writes:
>Use "ps -ef | grep defunct" and have a look at the third column of the
>output, which contains the PID's of the parent processes. Terminate or
>kill the parent processes and the zombies will go away. There is no
>other way to get rid of them if you don't have access to the source
>code of the programs generating the zombies.

This won't work.  The PPID of all the defunct processes will be 1.  A patch
for this problem is currently under test, and will be generally available
shortly.  If you're suffering from this problem then run this script from
cron about once an hour.  

#!/bin/ksh
ps -je | while read -u0 data
do
    set $data
    case $7 in
        T) kill -CONT $2 ;;
        *) ;;
    esac
done

This is only a work around, but you won't have to reboot the system every
day to get rid of them.  Then contact your local CSC, quote IPMT case number
UVO102126 and put your name down for the patch.

