>I'm new to OSF/1 having just got two DEC 3000/800Ss to look after and
>the ordered manuals have not arrived yet.

Keep 'em nice n warm.  Feed occasionally, and make sure they have a clean
litterbox.  They make great pets. 

>How do you set up remote printing? On the IBM RS6K you edit
>/etc/qconfig and then ask the sysadmin on the Vax to fix up that end.
>I want to print on a general university queue that is on the VAX
>to a line printer. How do you do this on the DEC?

Ahh, folks that have been polluted by aix.  :)  Umm, it's pretty
easy, actually.  OSF/1 has enough berkeley-isms to make it a trivial
matter.

Hack up an /etc/printcap file to look something like this:

vaxptr|Remote printer on the Vax:\
	:rp=remoteprintername:\
	:rm=remotevaxname:\
	:sd=/var/spool/remoteprintername

Do an 'lpstat -t', and see if the Alpha connects to the remote lpd and
shows queue entries.

NOW - i'm making assumptions here - i'm assuming the vax is running
some version of the berkeley lpd stuff and can accept queries and
jobs in that manner.  May be an off assumpiton, but we use this
mechanism to print to remote Sun printers (which, obviously, can
handle remote lpd stuff)

