Scott Ruch (swr@swell.unx.dec.com) wrote:
: I used to see this error when I didn't have the kernel configured correctly.
: You need the packetfilter enabled to use the SoftNode ethernet driver. You
: also need the CDFS filesystem enabled to use the CDrom from SoftWindows.  I
: found all of this in the SoftWindows setup manual - good reading!

I discussed this off-line with the poster of the original question.  For those
of you without access to OSF/1 or SoftWindows documentation, here's a synopsis 
of what you have to do to add the packetfilter and CDFS to your kernel:

To add the packetfilter to your kernel, you have to edit your system's
configuration file.  As root, do the following:

	- Edit /sys/conf/<machine_name> and add the following line:

		options PACKETFILTER

	- Run 'doconfig -c <machine_name>' and answer "no" when it asks
	  you if you want to edit the config file (you just did this!)

	- Doconfig will build a new kernel with the packetfilter enabled
	  and tell you that the new kernel is in /sys/<machine_name>/vmunix.

	- copy (don't 'mv') this kernel to /vmunix and reboot the system.

If you have a CD-rom and want to use that from SoftWindows, you need to add
"options CDFS" as well.

