R. David Murray <rdmurray@keene.edu> wrote:
> My biggest question is, why would this noise source affect NFS so strongly,
> yet leave, for example, telnet terminal sessions (across the same segment
> the NFS traffic was traversing) performing apparently normally?

NFS is optimised for low latency low noise high throughput links. For an
extreme case, telnet works fine over a PPP link via a 14.4k modem, but NFS
times out just trying to do the initial mount.

You may not be able to make NFS as robust as you want, no matter how you
tune it.
