In article <34aask$t85@cismsun.univ-lyon1.fr>, buffat@europe.mecaflu.ec-lyon.fr (Buffat Marc) writes:
|> are there a version of gprof for DEC ALPHA. I want to use it for the
|> profiling of C and C++ program. I dont like prof and I need the
|> call graph profil
|> Thanks in advance

Aside from the Atom version of gprof that Dirk Grunwald mentioned, there is
also a native version of gprof in OSF/1 V3.0.  The native version works the
same as on other systems.  Compile with -pg and then use the gprof utility.
The gprof(1) manpage has more details.  Gprof is able to report time and
call graph information for library calls to libc.a and libm.a as long as you
link -non_shared (do not use shared libraries).  Unfortunately, gprof is not
yet supported for C++, but support will be available in V1.3B of the C++
compiler which will ship at the end of this month.  Gprof support is available
now in the C compiler.


