We couldn't handle SMP at all under OSF/1 until recently, so there was
some credibility to these claims in the past. Of course, this isn't true
anymore since OSF/1 V3.0 is out. The compilers that do
automatic decomposition have been out for some time on VMS, so they are
well tested (it's the same GEM compilers on all the platforms).

As to quality of the SMP implementation, people tend to look at how
well it "scales":

First, some data from John DiMarcos SPEC table (the entries for the
SPARCcenter 1000 & 2000 are very old, does anybody have newer ones ?):

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
