Of course you can't kill a dead process :-)

Use "ps -ef | grep defunct" and have a look at the third column of the
output, which contains the PID's of the parent processes. Terminate or
kill the parent processes and the zombies will go away. There is no
other way to get rid of them if you don't have access to the source
code of the programs generating the zombies.

