>out from OSF. On HPUX this is simply done by running "ppl"; is there an
>equivalent hidden somewhere on OSF?
>
>Mac.

The only solution I've found is to set up UUCP, program the modem to
ignore DTR, then use uucico to make the call and negotiate the login for
you.  Then run slattach and set up your routing. Sure, it's a waste of bus
cycles and a kluge.  But, the number of keystrokes required to SLIP
connect is minimized. 

Another caveat: when you want to break the connection, the other side must
hang up first or you must cycle power on the modem or you can hammer the
tty with ATH's. 

Email me if you need help with the above.

Now, a question: 

Has anyone been able to use the second SLIP interface, slp1? 

We're running OSF/1 v2.0 on a DEC Flamingo (model 500).


