  Never heard about this CD-ROM - anyway, if you are sure it is bootable but the
boot fails with this dumb message : "84: fail", it may be caused by the SCSI bus
taking too much time to reset at the beginning of the boot phase, and preventing
a correct access to the CD-ROM drive.

  To modify this behavior, set the SCSI reset delay to at least 4 seconds :
while in console mode, type in :

>>> SET SCSI_RESET 4

	Hope this helps.

