  First, it is useless to save a truncated crash file, as you will not be
able to use it afterward.

  Second, a possible answer to you question, from 'man savecore', is :

	savecore [-cefv] directory [system]
	-c	    Does not copy the dump, but	simply marks it	invalid.

  You can change the savecore parameters in the /sbin/init.d/savecore file.

