|>
|>A small voice at the back is asking me what happens next when the client
|>manages to run the boot file I send it. How does it get the rest of the OS?
|>

The kernels you are using are not network bootable.  In V3.0 (where dataless 
systems are supported), the doconfig command will allow you to create a network
bootable kernel.  doconfig utilizes the pmerge command to prepend the "sboot"
bootfile to the resultant kernel to create a network bootable version of the
kernel.

Neither pmerge or sboot are available on releases prior to V3.0.

Dave


