Is 3.0 out yet ? I accept that DEC OSF/1 is not exactly the same as
OSF/1 (vendor-adaption was one of the goals of OSF). However, mentioning
OSF/1 1.3 vs. 1.2 I mainly pointed to the difference between a Mach 2.5
Quasi-BSD Kernel vs. a Mach 3.0 real microkernel with OSF beeing a server
on it. This difference lets 1.3 introduce the concept of sparse filled
address spaces, which is the only _real_ way to allow free() to give
memory back to the system. The probability that one can lower the break
on a random free() is not that high - even with sorted pools. Thats a
problem which is immanent to the linear-extended address space concept.

