A couple of weeks back, I posted regarding the inability to add a remotely
mounted filesystem to an Xserver font path under OSF/1 2.0.  The problem is
caused by the X server generating malformed RPC requests when it attempts
to read the remotely mounted filesystem (in particular, they identify the
server as being a member of 32 groups, all with gid 0).  The fix, thanks to
Ric Werme of DEC, is to comment out the line in /usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf
that relates to the server's display postscript extension.  

Marc



