>
>I am interested in being able to boot an Alpha AXP 3000/300X from across
>the network...
>
>I have tried using vmunix, genvmunix and even osf_boot as the bootfile from 
>both versions 1.3 and 2.0 but still get no joy.
>

What the Alpha (and DECstations too, for that matter) is doing at boot
time is setting up a RAM disk and loading a disk image into it from the
file you specified.  Thus, you need to have a version of vmunix that
knows about RAM disks.

On Ultrix, you get this from the RIS subset.  I have no idea where to get
such a beast for OSF, since there is no RIS subset.  We got ours from
a DECathena subset.

The one thing I wish DEC would do is give us some tools to build such a
disk image for ourselves.  We HATE the .profile that DEC includes in their
image.  It confuses the heck out of our users.
