driver, I have added the following explanation to the README.osf file,
which explains the problem and the fix.

IMPORTANT NOTE:  This is a STREAMS-based kernel driver.  tty drivers
corresponding to physical devices do NOT support STREAMS under DEC OSF/1
(at least in the current version) --- don't ask me why not, I have
absolutely no clue.  This code works fine on a pty, such as a pty openned
by a network connection from, say, a central dialin facility.  There
is a work-around if you want to use a physical port for your PPP connection
(such as a directly connected modem).  After making the initial connection
over the physical line, perform an rlogin as yourself on that line.  The
rlogin connection operates through a pty, so no you can run PPP from your
rlogged-in process.  Yes it's a pain, but don't bug me --- ask DEC why
STREAMS are only partially supported under OSF/1.


