>be worked out. Let's hope.
>
>BTW: Accler8 sells OPEN TPU. It's a repackaged nuTPU.
>

That's all true.  I've used nu/TPU over about two or three years now on
Suns and the various bugs are really annoying.  It is much more than
what Larry mentions.  For most work you won't really notice much but as
soon as you use slightly more enhanced features (e.g. set left margin to
something other than 1) the thing is soon unusable.  The most annoying
thing I encounter occasionally is that it can't handle its journal file
properly.  In a revocer run it can't rewrite it and you may end up with
an empty .tjl file.  This will prevent tpu from writing a new one in
your next session.  And the buffering of this file is such that it is
left empty most of the time anyway.  Very annoying with the unreliable
connections here.

Nevertheless, it is still the best tpu you can get on Unix.  But you'll
need at least an emtpy Sparc 2 if you want to edit slightly bigger
files.  It is also a CPU hog.

Michael
