Before OSF V3.0 I don't think the RZ57 was supported on any of the
AXP systems.  I think this was a case of not being supporte because
it failed qualification.  For V3.0 I think it is support with the
right firmware upgrade, but I don't a V3.0 SPD handy to check.

>
># mount /dev/rz5d /mnt
>/dev/rz5d on /mnt: No such device or address

One problem you're probably having is that the RZ57 probably won't
be rz5.  Most (all?) of the 3000 series have two SCSI adapters, one
for internal devices and one for external devices.  Target 0-6 are the
internal devices and targets 8-14 are the external devices.  If the
target ID of the RZ57 was 5, then it will most likely be rz13 on your
AXP system.

>
>which is very strange, because the /dev/rz5? and /dev/rrz5? devices
>exist. 
>There are three entries for rz5 in the GENERIC-kernel:
>device disk             rz5     at asc0         drive 40

For what its worth, asc is the controller used on the 3000 systems.

>device disk             rz5     at siop0        drive 40
>device disk             rz5     at skz0         drive 40

The siop is used on the DEC 4000 and skz is one of the SCSI
channels of the KZMSA used on the DEC 7000/10000.
 
