>As far as I know it still comes with C.

Well, not really.  Yes, a C compiler is present if you have the base
OSF/1 system, but it is supposed to be used only for rebuilding the
kernel.  You can't use the debugger with just a base license.

In order to use a C compiler for development, you are supposed to buy
the "Developer's toolkit" option.  Among other things, this gets you
DEC C, the high-performance ANSI-C compiler which is what we use
for performance benchmarks and which is compatible with DEC C on
other platforms.  This compiler is accessed by "cc -migrate".

