Here's what the Software Product Description for DEC OSF/1 AXP says:

 The DEC OSF/1 Operating System license provides a licensed user the
 right to use the software as described within this Software Product
 Description. Separate licenses are available for the right to use de-
 velopment tools and the C compiler, and separate licenses are avail-
 able for the right to use the Remote Installation Service. Refer to
 the Software Product Descriptions for the DEC OSF/1 Developers' Ex-
 tensions (SPD 44.36.xx) and the DEC OSF/1 Server Extensions (SPD 44.35.xx)
 for descriptions and details.

I'm not qualified to make a legal interpretation of Digital policies, but
my personal take on this is that if you don't have the Developer's Extensions
license, you're not licensed to use the C compiler.  You'll find that other
UNIX vendors have similar arrangements.
